{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["The 'Largest single contribution' metric (metrics.3) is not a meaningful entropy quantity and is not tied to any source claim; it adds cosmetic completeness without scientific value. More importantly, the lesson's core claim 'uniform maximizes entropy for fixed n' is never actually verified numerically — the code only reports log₂n as a reference. Replace metrics.3 with a genuine check: the entropy gap H_uniform − H (nonnegative, zero iff uniform), which directly tests the maximization claim and changes with every input.", "The compute function silently coerces negative or non-finite raw entries to 0 (x > 0 ? x : 0). The control declares min:0, so negative entries are out of domain, but the coercion means a user typing a negative value gets a silently different distribution rather than a clamped/flagged one. Since the schema constrains min:0, this is acceptable, but the normalization branch when total===0 (all entries zero) maps to uniform 1/n, which contradicts the stated 'certain outcome' semantics and is not documented. Document this fallback in the message/steps so the displayed probabilities are not misleading.", "The exploration 'Skewed distribution versus uniform' instructs the learner to 'change the first entry toward 0.25 while keeping the others equal' but the control is a single vector with no per-entry guidance; with normalization, moving p1 toward 0.25 while others stay at 0.1 does not keep the others equal after normalization. The action is not executable as written and the observe claim ('H rises toward 2 bits') is only true if the others are renormalized to (1−p1)/3. Reword the action to specify editing all four entries to approach [0.25,0.25,0.25,0.25]."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "Certain outcome, n=4", "state": {"probs": [1, 0, 0, 0]}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.1.value", "value": 2, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 2, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Uniform n=4", "state": {"probs": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25]}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "value": 2, "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Skewed [0.7,0.1,0.1,0.1]", "state": {"probs": [0.7, 0.1, 0.1, 0.1]}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "formula": "-(0.7*Math.log2(0.7)+3*0.1*Math.log2(0.1))", "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "formula": "2+(0.7*Math.log2(0.7)+3*0.1*Math.log2(0.1))", "atol": 1e-12}]}, {"name": "Edge: all-zero raw entries fall back to uniform", "state": {"probs": [0, 0, 0]}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.0.value", "formula": "Math.log2(3)", "atol": 1e-12}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 0, "atol": 1e-12}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Entropy bounded by uniform maximum", "expression": "o.metrics[0].value === null || o.metrics[1].value === null || (o.metrics[0].value <= o.metrics[1].value + 1e-9)"}, {"name": "Gap equals uniform minus entropy and is nonnegative", "expression": "o.metrics[3].value === null || o.metrics[0].value === null || o.metrics[1].value === null || (Math.abs(o.metrics[3].value - (o.metrics[1].value - o.metrics[0].value)) < 1e-9 && o.metrics[3].value >= -1e-9)"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 79.1}
